abstract: >-
  Token on Me (TOM) gives the token-level authorship of the code of [[tom: projects]]
  free and open-source projects with 1,000 commits or more whose largest
  programming language is C, C++, Java or Rust ([[tom: rows]] token rows). cregit
  makes the attribution with git blame at the token level. The identities are
  pseudonymized. Organization columns give the organization of the address of
  each author and of the account of each project, and the organization tables
  are part of the dataset.
keywords:
  - mining software repositories
  - authorship
  - cregit
  - open source
  - organizations
